{"retractions" [[17592186354979 :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A.$ Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$"] [17592186354979 :question/worked-solution "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186354981 17592186354982 17592186354983 17592186354984 17592186354985] "immutable_fields" [[17592186354980 :answer-field/id] [17592186354980 :answer-field/key] [17592186354980 :answer-field/type] [17592186354980 :answer-field/correct] [17592186354980 :answer-field/choices]]}
